# counter/_websocket scope 100 — parse the message.
#
# Each complete WebSocket message the browser sends is ONE run of this
# stack, entering at scope 0 with the text on `@websocket.msg.text` (a
# binary frame would arrive base64 on `@websocket.msg.data`). The parsed
# object lands at `.msg` — a bare author path, since `_txc.*` is the
# chassis control plane. Invalid JSON fails this EMIT, `.msg` stays absent,
# and 300/unknown.txcl answers.
WHEN @websocket.phase == "message"
  EMIT .msg = &json(@websocket.msg.text)
